[SUCCESS]⎿ [{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have comprehensive information. Let me create a complete report based on my analysis:\n\n## Comprehensive Analysis of Cart/Checkout/Order REST Resources and I3.T2 Task Status\n\nBased on my thorough examination of the codebase, I've compiled a detailed analysis of the current state and what's needed for task I3.T2.\n\n### 1. **Existing REST Resource Classes**\n\nThree main REST resources exist in `/modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/api/rest/`:\n\n**CartResource.java** (Incomplete OpenAPI annotations)\n- Path: `/api/v1/cart`\n- Endpoints:\n  - `GET /cart` - Get current cart (no OpenAPI annotations)\n  - `DELETE /cart` - Clear cart (no OpenAPI annotations)\n  - `POST /cart/items` - Add item to cart (no OpenAPI annotations)\n  - `PATCH /cart/items/{itemId}` - Update cart item quantity (no OpenAPI annotations)\n  - `DELETE /cart/items/{itemId}` - Remove cart item (no OpenAPI annotations)\n- Status: **Functional but lacks OpenAPI @Operation, @APIResponse, @Tag annotations**\n- Uses: CustomSessionContext for guest/auth carts, Problem Details for errors (inline implementation)\n- Handles: Optimistic locking (OptimisticLockException), validation, idempotency via session cookies/headers\n\n**CheckoutResource.java** (Complete with OpenAPI annotations)\n- Path: `/api/v1/checkout`\n- Endpoints:\n  - `POST /checkout/commit` - Complete checkout and create order (201 Created response)\n- Status: **Complete with full OpenAPI annotations**\n- Annotations present:\n  - `@Tag(name = \"Storefront\", description = \"Customer-facing checkout operations\")`\n  - `@Operation` with detailed description\n  - `@APIResponses` covering 201, 400, 402, 409, 503 status codes\n  - `@Parameter` for X-Idempotency-Key header validation\n- Features:\n  - Idempotency key validation (UUID format check)\n  - Feature flag check (checkout.order-creation.enabled) \n  - Uses CheckoutSaga for orchestration\n  - ProblemDetailsUtil for consistent error responses\n  - Handles: IdempotencyConflictException, CheckoutDisabledException, IllegalArgumentException, general RuntimeException\n\n**OrderResource.java** (Partially annotated - missing OpenAPI)\n- Path: `/api/v1` (split into storefront and admin endpoints)\n- Storefront endpoints:\n  - `GET /orders/{orderId}` - Get order details\n  - `GET /orders` - List orders with pagination (page, pageSize, status filters)\n- Admin endpoints:\n  - `GET /admin/orders` - List all tenant orders with advanced filtering\n  - `GET /admin/orders/{orderId}` - Get order details (admin)\n  - `PATCH /admin/orders/{orderId}` - Update order (status, notes, tags)\n  - `POST /admin/orders/{orderId}/cancel` - Cancel order (requires reason)\n  - `POST /admin/orders/{orderId}/refund` - Refund order (requires X-Idempotency-Key, amount, reason, optional restock flag)\n- Status: **No OpenAPI annotations anywhere - completely missing**\n- Features:\n  - Problem Details inline implementation (duplicated from CartResource)\n  - Supports optimistic locking exception handling\n  - Metadata JSON handling for notes/tags\n  - Pagination support\n- Gaps: TODOs at lines 104, 138, 206 for authorization, user filtering, and role annotations\n\n### 2. **Missing OpenAPI Annotations Summary**\n\n| Resource | Annotation Status | Details |\n|----------|------------------|---------|\n| CartResource | Missing | No @Tag, @Operation, @APIResponse annotations on any method |\n| CheckoutResource | Complete | All methods fully annotated |\n| OrderResource | Missing | No annotations on any storefront or admin endpoint |\n\n### 3. **API Type Classes Status** \n\nThe following DTO types are defined but NOT referenced by any OpenAPI path specifications:\n\n**Request DTOs (partially created):**\n- `ApplyPromotionRequest.java` - For applying promo codes to cart\n- `CancelOrderRequest.java` - For cancelling orders\n- `RefundOrderRequest.java` - For refunding orders (includes Money amount, reason, restockItems flag)\n- `PromotionRequest.java` - For creating/updating promotions (POST/PATCH admin endpoints)\n- `CheckoutCommitRequest.java` - For checkout commit\n\n**Response DTOs (created):**\n- `CheckoutResponse.java` - Returns orderId, orderNumber, paymentIntentId, status, totalAmount, currency, paidAt\n- `CartListResponse.java` - Paginated response with items + pagination metadata\n- `OrderListResponse.java` - Paginated response with OrderSummary items + pagination metadata\n- `OrderSummary.java` - Lightweight order representation for lists\n- `PromotionDto.java` - Full promotion details with discount config, usage stats\n- `PromotionListResponse.java` - Paginated promotion list response\n- `RefundResponse.java` - Refund result with refundId, amount, status, timestamps\n\n**Support DTOs:**\n- `ProblemDetailsUtil.java` - Utility class providing RFC 7807 error formatting with convenience methods:\n  - `badRequest()`, `unauthorized()`, `notFound()`, `conflict()`, `internalServerError()`, `serviceUnavailable()`\n  - Used only in CheckoutResource; OrderResource and CartResource have inline implementations\n\n### 4. **Promotion API Status**\n\n**CRITICAL GAP:** No promotion REST resource class exists at all!\n\nFrom OpenAPI spec and DTOs, the following promotion endpoints are defined but NOT implemented:\n- `POST /api/v1/admin/promotions` - Create promotion\n- `GET /api/v1/admin/promotions` - List promotions (with pagination)\n- `GET /api/v1/admin/promotions/{promotionId}` - Get single promotion\n- `PATCH /api/v1/admin/promotions/{promotionId}` - Update promotion\n- `DELETE /api/v1/admin/promotions/{promotionId}` - Delete/archive promotion\n- `POST /api/v1/cart/promotions` or `POST /api/v1/cart/apply-promo` - Apply promotion to cart\n\n### 5. **Admin Cart Management**\n\n**CRITICAL GAP:** No admin cart management endpoints exist!\n\nThe OpenAPI spec references but no implementation exists:\n- `GET /api/v1/admin/carts` - List all carts (with filtering by status, customer, date)\n- Potentially: `DELETE /api/v1/admin/carts/{cartId}` - Admin cart cancellation\n\n### 6. **Detailed Issues by Resource**\n\n#### CartResource Issues:\n1. **Missing OpenAPI annotations** - No @Tag, @Operation, @APIResponse, @Parameter annotations\n2. **Problem Details duplication** - Private `createProblemDetails()` method duplicates ProblemDetailsUtil\n3. **No admin endpoints** - Should have `/admin/carts` list endpoint\n4. **No promotion apply endpoint** - Should support POST /cart/apply-promo or POST /cart/promotions\n5. **Session management outside scope** - Session ID via header OR cookie, but no explicit feature flag configuration\n\n#### CheckoutResource Strengths:\n1. **Fully annotated** - Complete OpenAPI contract with proper response codes\n2. **Idempotency support** - X-Idempotency-Key header validation and exception handling\n3. **Feature flag integration** - CheckoutDisabledException for feature gating\n4. **Proper error responses** - Uses ProblemDetailsUtil for consistency\n5. **Location header** - Returns 201 with Location: /api/v1/orders/{orderId}\n\n#### OrderResource Issues:\n1. **Complete absence of OpenAPI annotations** - No @Operation, @APIResponse, @Parameter annotations\n2. **Missing admin security annotations** - TODO comment at line 206 for @RolesAllowed\n3. **Missing user authorization** - TODO at line 104 and 138 for customer self-service scope checks\n4. **Duplicated Problem Details** - `createProblemDetails()` inline implementation\n5. **JSON handling code smell** - Direct ObjectNode manipulation instead of using typed DTOs\n6. **Placeholder refund implementation** - TODO at line 445, returns mock data instead of actual refund logic\n7. **Inconsistent response format** - Returns Maps instead of typed OrderListResponse/OrderSummary DTOs\n8. **Missing pagination validation** - No max pageSize enforcement, accepts arbitrary values\n9. **No response DTOs** - Should return OrderListResponse and OrderSummary, but uses HashMap instead\n\n### 7. **What's Missing for I3.T2**\n\nBased on the task description: *\"Extend OpenAPI + REST controllers for cart/checkout/order endpoints (storefront + admin), including ProblemDetails, rate limits, and webhook callback modeling\"*\n\n**MUST IMPLEMENT:**\n\n1. **Add OpenAPI annotations to CartResource**\n   - @Tag on class\n   - @Operation on each method\n   - @APIResponse for success and error codes\n   - @Parameter for path/query/header params\n\n2. **Add OpenAPI annotations to OrderResource**\n   - @Tag on class\n   - @Operation on each endpoint\n   - @APIResponse covering 200, 404, 409, 500 status codes\n   - @Parameter definitions\n   - Proper response schema references\n\n3. **Extract/consolidate ProblemDetails utility**\n   - CartResource and OrderResource should use `ProblemDetailsUtil` instead of duplicating\n   - Already implemented in `ProblemDetailsUtil.java`\n\n4. **Create PromotionResource class** with:\n   - `GET /admin/promotions` - list with pagination\n   - `POST /admin/promotions` - create\n   - `GET /admin/promotions/{id}` - get single\n   - `PATCH /admin/promotions/{id}` - update\n   - `DELETE /admin/promotions/{id}` - soft delete\n   - Full OpenAPI annotations\n   - Uses PromotionDto, PromotionRequest, PromotionListResponse DTOs (all exist)\n\n5. **Add cart promotion endpoint**\n   - `POST /api/v1/cart/promotions` or `/api/v1/cart/apply-promo`\n   - Request: ApplyPromotionRequest (exists)\n   - Response: Updated CartDto with discount applied\n   - Full OpenAPI annotations\n\n6. **Add admin cart management**\n   - `GET /api/v1/admin/carts` - paginated list with filters\n   - Response: CartListResponse (exists)\n   - Full OpenAPI annotations\n   - Filtering by status, customer email, date range\n\n7. **Security annotations**\n   - Add @RolesAllowed or equivalent for admin endpoints\n   - Customer authorization checks for storefront endpoints (self-service orders)\n\n8. **Complete OrderResource refund logic**\n   - Replace TODO placeholder with actual Payment service integration\n   - Return typed RefundResponse (exists)\n   - Proper idempotency handling\n\n9. **Response type consistency**\n   - OrderResource should return OrderListResponse instead of Map\n   - OrderResource should return OrderSummary items\n   - Already have the DTOs, just need to use them\n\n10. **Rate limiting metadata**\n    - Add response headers for X-RateLimit-* information\n    - May require interceptor/filter support\n\n11. **Webhook modeling in OpenAPI**\n    - Document Stripe webhook callbacks\n    - Carrier webhook callbacks\n    - Already have PaymentWebhookResource but needs OpenAPI documentation\n\n### 8. **Test Requirements for I3.T2**\n\nThe acceptance criteria states: *\"controllers use TenantContext & feature flags; e2e stub uses RestAssured to run sample checkout\"*\n\nMissing test coverage for:\n- Promotion CRUD operations with proper validation\n- Promotion application to cart\n- Admin cart listing and management\n- Authorization enforcement on admin endpoints\n- Feature flag gating (already in CheckoutResource, needed in others)\n- Order refund completion via payment service\n- E2E integration tests using RestAssured\n\n### Summary\n\n**What Exists and Works:**\n- CheckoutResource: Fully functional with complete OpenAPI spec\n- CartResource: Functional but needs OpenAPI annotations\n- OrderResource: Functional but needs OpenAPI annotations + security + proper DTOs\n- ProblemDetailsUtil: Reusable utility (CheckoutResource uses it; others should too)\n- All API type DTOs: Completely defined except no usage\n\n**What's Missing (Blockers for I3.T2):**\n1. PromotionResource class entirely missing\n2. OpenAPI annotations on CartResource and OrderResource\n3. Admin cart management endpoint missing\n4. Cart promotion apply endpoint missing\n5. OrderResource refund logic still a placeholder\n6. Security/authorization annotations missing across all resources\n7. E2E integration tests with RestAssured"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ae0adab (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]
